00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:48.959
Stefano Gogioso: Into your succinct, proof system.

142
00:25:48.960 --> 00:26:12.979
Stefano Gogioso: That involves a bunch of things. The actual circuit execution itself is the smallest part of it. Most of the complexity goes into the fact that you have hashes every time. Yeah, like, every time you have a nonlinear gate, you have to absorb state into a… you have to absorb it into a hash state, and that is what ultimately gives you the Fiat Shamir commitment, and all of that is what's expensive.

